# Android shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# Git's default `autocrlf` converts them to CRLF on checkout, and Android's sh cannot parse
# a `\r`: the module's service.sh failed with "syntax error: unexpected 'do'" and the module
# silently did nothing at boot, while the same script ran correctly when invoked by hand
# from a push. Pinning the endings here stops that from coming back on a fresh clone.
*.sh            text eol=lf

# Shell scripts without the extension, in the KernelSU module and native helpers.
module/post-fs-data.sh   text eol=lf
module/service.sh        text eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.ko            binary
*.so            binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary

# Python and Markdown are ordinary text; LF is fine everywhere.
*.py            text
*.md            text
*.txt           text
*.yml           text
*.yaml          text
*.toml          text
